  "conclusions": [
    "250 g in-plane is the only clearly safe case (16.3 MPa at 75 g).",
    "250 g out-of-plane is marginal (35.1 MPa at 75 g); a 1 mm boss/washer is advised.",
    "500 g out-of-plane fails PLA bulk strength (70.2 MPa at 75 g).",
    "If the whole 183 g quad hangs from these four points, even 250 g out-of-plane is 85.7 MPa; do not use the thin half-holes as the only load path."
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Do not route the battery strap through the thin half-hole as the only load path.",
    "Add a 2 mm local boss/ring around the half-hole end, or a 1 mm aluminum plate under the strap.",
    "Increase the edge ligament from 1.16 mm to >=2.5 mm by moving the slot inward or extending the plate locally.",
    "Fillet the slot-to-edge transition; sharp re-entrant geometry concentrates stress.",
    "Use a separate strap bar on the bottom plate or route the strap around the plate."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "quasi-static equivalent load, not a transient drop/contact simulation",
    "isotropic PLA screening; printed layer direction and defects are not measured",
    "strap contact and friction are not modelled; the load is distributed over the half-hole wall nodes",
    "the 1.16 mm ligament is resolved by ~2-3 elements; refine locally for a final design"
  ]
